>Larson</surname><given-names>EW</given-names></name><name><surname>Edwards</surname><given-names>WD</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Risk factors for aortic dissection: a necropsy study of 161 cases</article-title><source><italic>American Journal of Cardiology</italic></source><year>1984</year><volume>53</volume><issue>6</issue><fpage>849</fpage><lpage>855</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="other">2-s2.0-0021332547</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">6702637</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B8"><label>8</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Klompas</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Does this patient have an acute thoracic aortic dissection?</article-title><source><italic>Journal of the American Medical Association</italic></source><year>2002</year><volume>287</volume><issue>17</issue><fpage>2262</fpage><lpage>2272</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="other">2-s2.0-0036570101</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11980527</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B9"><label>9</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Pi&#x000ea;tre</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Von Segesser</surname><given-names>LK</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Aortic dissection</article-title><source><italic>Lancet</italic></source><year>1997</year><volume>349</volume><issue>9063</issue><fpage>1461</fpage><lpage>1464</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="other">2-s2.0-0343376114</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9164331</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B10"><label>10</label><element-citation publication-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dahnert</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Cardiovascular disorders : aortic dissection</article-title><source><italic>Radiology Review Manual</italic></source><year>2003</year><edition>5 th edition</edition><publisher-loc>Pa</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Lippincott Williams &#x00026; Wilkins</publisher-name><fpage>607</fpage><lpage>609</lpage></element-citation></ref><ref id="B11"><label>11</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Casta&#x000f1;er</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Andreu</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Gallardo</surname><given-names>X</given-names></name><name><surname>Mata</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><name><surname>Cabezuelo</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name><name><surname>Pallard&#x000f3;</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>CT in nontraumatic acute thoracic aortic disease: typical and atypicalfeatures and complications</article-title><source><italic>Radiographics</italic></source><year>2003</year><volume>23</volume><fpage>S93</fpage><lpage>S110</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="other">2-s2.0-0346786505</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14557505</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B12"><label>12</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Karmy-Jones</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Aldea</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Boyle</surname><given-names>EM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The continuing evolution in the management of thoracic aortic dissection</article-title><source><italic>Chest</italic></source><year>2000</year><volume>117</volume><issue>5</issue><fpage>1221</fpage><lpage>1223</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="other">2-s2.0-0034035227</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10807801</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B13"><label>13</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ramanath</surname><given-names>VS</given-names></